        <p>Spain's Non-Lucrative Visa and Digital Nomad Visa are designed for completely different people. The key distinction is simple: Can you work remotely in Spain?</p>
      </div>

      <p><strong>Non-Lucrative Visa (NLV):</strong> For people with independent income who do NOT want to work in Spain. This is for retirees, early-stage investors, people with pensions, those with investment income, or anyone with passive income sources. If you're earning money during your time in Spain, the NLV is not for you.</p>

      <p><strong>Digital Nomad Visa (DNV):</strong> For remote workers who earn income online while living in Spain. If you work for non-Spanish companies, run an international freelance business, or manage non-Spanish income sources, the DNV is your visa. You're explicitly permitted to work; in fact, the visa is designed around remote work.</p>

      <p>The choice is straightforward: Do you need to work in Spain? If yes, Digital Nomad. If no, Non-Lucrative. Everything else flows from this single question.</p>

